4)Version History ⭐
        SharePoint can keep previous versions when a document changes.
        You can see who changed it, view older versions, and restore a previous version. How versioning works in lists and libraries
        
                Example:
                        Budget.docx
                        Version 1 → Vinod uploaded
                        Version 2 → Manager modified
                        Version 3 → Finance updated
                        
                If Version 3 is wrong, you can restore an earlier version.

5)Check-out / Check-in
        A document can be checked out while someone is working on it.
        Check-in puts the updated document back into the controlled library process. Plan document versioning, content approval,
        and check-out controls in SharePoint
            1)Check-out:
                    Suppose this file is in a SharePoint Document Library:
                    BudgetApproval.docx
                    Normally, multiple people may be able to edit Office documents together.
                    But imagine you want:
                    "I am making an important change. I don't want anyone else editing this document until I finish."
                    
                    You Check out the file.
                    Once checked out:
                    
                            The file stays in the library.
                            It is marked as checked out to you.
                            You get exclusive editing rights.
                            Other users cannot edit it until you check it back in
                2)Check in:
                        Once Vinod finishes, he selects:
                        ... → Check in
                        He can also enter a comment such as:
                        "Updated maximum budget from $10,000 to $15,000."
                        
                        After check-in:
                        🔓 The document is available again for other users with appropriate permissions to edit.
                        
                        So:
                        Check out → Edit → Save → Check in
